// URL-loaded customization: enableNewSplit
//
// Enables metadata-driven display set splitting: series instances are split
// into display sets by the @cornerstonejs/metadata split-rules engine
// (`useMetadataDisplaySet` customization) instead of the stack SOP class
// handler.  Instances not matched by any split rule (video, whole-slide,
// ECG, SEG, SR, RT, PDF, ...) still go through the registered SOP class
// handlers, so specialized extensions keep working unchanged.
//
// The default rules include `mixedDimensionalityBValue`, which splits MR
// series mixing instances with and without DiffusionBValue into separate
// display sets (the DWI mixed-b-value issue).
//
// The default rule `singleImageModality` is off, so a CR, DX or MG series is
// one display set, and not one display set for each image as with the stack
// SOP class handler. `split/dxCrSingleImages.jsonc` shows a per-image split
// for small DX and CR series as a rule.
//
// Load it with `?customization=split/enableNewSplit`.
//
// Custom rules are @cornerstonejs/metadata raw selector data (conditions,
// `{ "expression": "..." }`, series facts) - see `split/scoutSeries.jsonc` for
// a complete example.  `splitRules` is keyed by
// rule id: add a rule with `$merge`.  Rules are evaluated in ascending
// `priority` with first-match-wins per instance.  The default rules use the
// priorities 1..n, so a priority below 0 runs before every default rule, a
// priority above 10000 runs after every default rule (it only sees instances
// no default rule matched), and a priority of null turns a rule off.
{
  "global": {
    "useMetadataDisplaySet": { "enabled": { "$set": true } }
  }
}
